From b1a8fdd39de6b63b30ed7ba2414a41250db85d7b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam Krawczyk <adam.krawczyk0698@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Mar 2026 09:29:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: store provider API keys in provider-keys.json, not
 openclaw.json

Provider keys were written to config.providers in openclaw.json,
which newer OpenClaw rejects as unrecognized. Broke all clients
who added their own API key (e.g. Google AI Studio) via the board.

- New ~/.openclaw/provider-keys.json stores BYOK API keys
- Keys synced to env vars (GEMINI_API_KEY etc) on startup
- Auto-migration from legacy config.providers on first load
- entrypoint.sh handles migration before board starts

Fixes: Mariusz Krawczyk agent broken after adding Google key
---
